{
  "schema": 1,
  "name": "Collection companions without a creature template can be summoned and are named",
  "contract": "Companion spells from VanityCollection.dbc summon creatures that had no creature_template row; Creature::InitEntry refuses those, so the companion is never summoned, and 53 of the Sigil companions also had no collection model row, so the client's creature query went unanswered and the pet window showed no name or tooltip. Each summoned companion is its spell's creature, drawn with the display from the hertigservices/ascension-data creature cache at the companion scale of rev_20261009_60_companion_scale.sql (bounding box at most 1.2 yd tall and 1.8 yd long in the client's CreatureModelData/CreatureDisplayInfo). Dishu and Gilmorian already had a collection model row and are summon-only controls; the creature query for each of the 53 returns a response (rank 0) instead of the unknown-entry reply, which the metric ignores (-1). Stony Tark's display 14672 has other-gender display 14671 in creature_model_info, which the core picks half the time.",
  "timeout_ms": 300000,
